  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656092",
      "title": "Using Local References in Templates",
      "lectureOrder": 397,
      "videoOrder": 367,
      "sourceHash": "f901e0958075227e42c61b2e2bc5aae68900628e30c0444eee41f3578501c539",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 3.54,
          "en": "-: Back in the application we built",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.54,
          "end": 5.46,
          "en": "throughout the first lectures of this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.46,
          "end": 8.37,
          "en": "with our cockpit anti server element component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.37,
          "end": 11.31,
          "en": "with using output and input to pass data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.31,
          "end": 14.872,
          "en": "around our own custom property and event binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.872,
          "end": 17.22,
          "en": "Now, in the cockpit, right now I'm using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.22,
          "end": 20.52,
          "en": "two-way data binding to get the server name and content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.52,
          "end": 22.11,
          "en": "Now there's nothing wrong with it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.11,
          "end": 25.56,
          "en": "but maybe we don't need to use two-way data binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.56,
          "end": 29.73,
          "en": "Since I only want to save or use the data at the point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.73,
          "end": 32.16,
          "en": "of time I click the button the ad server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.16,
          "end": 34.68,
          "en": "or the ad server blueprint button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.68,
          "end": 36.93,
          "en": "it would be enough to get the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.93,
          "end": 39.63,
          "en": "of the input at this point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.63,
          "end": 43.74,
          "en": "and there is a nice way we can achieve just that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.74,
          "end": 47.67,
          "en": "So I'll duplicate this and comment out the old solution,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.67,
          "end": 51.33,
          "en": "and now I'll structure it out over a couple of lines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.33,
          "end": 53.7,
          "en": "and remove the two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.7,
          "end": 56.34,
          "en": "There and the other option we would have is to place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.34,
          "end": 59.01,
          "en": "a local reference on that element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.01,
          "end": 63.84,
          "en": "A local reference can be placed on any HTML element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.84,
          "end": 67.23,
          "en": "so not only on a input element, on anything you see here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.23,
          "end": 71.31,
          "en": "in the template, and you add with a hashtag and then a name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.31,
          "end": 74.85,
          "en": "of your choice, like for example, server name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.85,
          "end": 77.76,
          "en": "Since this is, well, what does this reference will hold?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.76,
          "end": 79.98,
          "en": "A reference to this element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.98,
          "end": 82.47,
          "en": "So maybe server name input. Now, important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.47,
          "end": 84.63,
          "en": "This reference, as I just said,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.63,
          "end": 87.39,
          "en": "will hold a reference to this element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.39,
          "end": 89.2,
          "en": "So not to devalue, we entered there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.239,
          "end": 93.47999999999999,
          "en": "to the whole HTML element with all its properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.47999999999999,
          "end": 98.47999999999999,
          "en": "We can see this, if we pass this now as an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.58,
          "end": 101.75999999999999,
          "en": "once we click at server on Add Server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.75999999999999,
          "end": 105.27000000000001,
          "en": "Here I can pass server name input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.27000000000001,
          "end": 107.19,
          "en": "because the other important thing you need to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.19,
          "end": 109.92,
          "en": "about references, besides how to create them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.92,
          "end": 113.28,
          "en": "is that you can use them everywhere in your template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.28,
          "end": 118.28,
          "en": "but, important, only there, not inside your TypeScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.07,
          "end": 122.16,
          "en": "only in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.16,
          "end": 123.96,
          "en": "But we do call the method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.96,
          "end": 125.91,
          "en": "inside the template, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.91,
          "end": 128.49,
          "en": "So here we can use server name input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.49,
          "end": 132.24,
          "en": "and that is a way how we can pass it to the types of code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.24,
          "end": 135.57,
          "en": "Because in on add server, we now know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.57,
          "end": 138,
          "en": "that we will receive the name input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138,
          "end": 140.31,
          "en": "You could also name it server name input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.31,
          "end": 143.13,
          "en": "And if we log this, we can analyze what this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.13,
          "end": 145.92000000000002,
          "en": "actually means, what we actually got here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.92000000000002,
          "end": 149.7,
          "en": "So let's save this and let our app reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.7,
          "end": 151.947,
          "en": "And, now if I test something and enter something here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.947,
          "end": 155.7,
          "en": "and I click add server, of course, this was broken here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.7,
          "end": 158.16,
          "en": "this is broken because we're not fetching the data correctly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.16,
          "end": 162.93,
          "en": "right now, you see we actually got the input element itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.93,
          "end": 166.14,
          "en": "So this SD element we got here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.14,
          "end": 169.65,
          "en": "that is what the local reference gives us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.65,
          "end": 172.32,
          "en": "the element with all its properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.32,
          "end": 176.31,
          "en": "So here we could also output value, the value of this input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.31,
          "end": 178.82999999999998,
          "en": "since we know that a input element has a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.82999999999998,
          "end": 180.03,
          "en": "-: And of course this will depend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.03,
          "end": 183.24,
          "en": "on which kind of element you placed your local reference on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.24,
          "end": 186.15,
          "en": "Not all elements have the same properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.15,
          "end": 188.94,
          "en": "So if this, if we try this again, you'd see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 188.94,
          "end": 193.02,
          "en": "we now print tests because we access the value of this input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 193.02,
          "end": 196.68,
          "en": "to which we got access through the local reference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.68,
          "end": 201.3,
          "en": "So, local references, a very nice feature to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.3,
          "end": 203.31,
          "en": "to some elements in your template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 203.31,
          "end": 205.95,
          "en": "and then use that either directly in the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.95,
          "end": 210.95,
          "en": "you could also output server name input value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 211.71,
          "end": 215.52,
          "en": "or you can pass it on like we do to use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.52,
          "end": 218.79,
          "en": "in a type script code, a nice and handy feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 218.79,
          "end": 221.34,
          "en": "Now with that being passed, we can use it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.34,
          "end": 226.2,
          "en": "to not only log our data to the console, but instead, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 226.2,
          "end": 229.65,
          "en": "once we define or once we create the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.65,
          "end": 232.8,
          "en": "we could access name, input, value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 232.8,
          "end": 234.93,
          "en": "And we should also be explicit about the type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.93,
          "end": 237.9,
          "en": "We know that this will be a HTML input element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.9,
          "end": 241.233,
          "en": "so we know that this value property will be there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 242.13,
          "end": 245.28,
          "en": "Same can of course be done on the blueprint,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 245.28,
          "end": 248.28,
          "en": "but we can also replace this new server name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 248.28,
          "end": 253.28,
          "en": "with name input and then value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 253.41,
          "end": 255.72,
          "en": "And with that we can get rid of new server name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 255.72,
          "end": 256.92,
          "en": "We don't need it anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 256.92,
          "end": 259.17,
          "en": "I will comment it out, so that we still have it there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 259.17,
          "end": 261.54,
          "en": "for reference, but the new approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 261.54,
          "end": 264.9,
          "en": "now only uses this local reference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 264.9,
          "end": 266.82,
          "en": "Now for this to work, we, of course, also need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 266.82,
          "end": 271.26,
          "en": "to pass this reference to our onAddBlueprint method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 271.26,
          "end": 273.723,
          "en": "So these are local references.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
